 "description": "<h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Bachelor of Arts</h3>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Film Major is a hybrid four-year program combining film theory, aesthetics, and practice. The program aims to graduate multi-skilled filmmakers, film practitioners, and researchers through comprehensive training and courses that adopt a cross-disciplinary approach to film theory and production, forming an integral vision of the film as a medium. The program offers extensive exposure to different film production crafts while staying up-to-date with the fast-changing film language. Our students are mentored by a team of masterful, award-winning, experienced, and diverse faculty of scholars, thinkers, filmmakers, and film practitioners who cover a wide range of disciplines in film studies and practice.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Knowledge exchange and cultural activities within the program are fostered through a solid local, regional, and international film-related network that also creates great opportunities for students to present their work locally and worldwide. Permanent interaction between students and faculty is highly encouraged and results in a dynamic learning environment that seeds the collective practice of filmmaking while motivating students to explore their singular cinematic voices.</p>\r\n\r\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Declaration Policy</strong></h4>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">A minimum grade of B in <a href=\"#\" class=\"permalink\" data-permalink_id=\"59746\" data-legacy_id=\"242\" data-signature=\"70ce1ccd0250f0d582948a3513dc7c9d\" data-display_type=\"tooltip\" data-link_text=\"%prefix% %code%\" data-anchor_text=\"\" data-from_id=\"5008\" data-from_type=\"program\" data-to_id=\"61555\" data-to_type=\"course\" data-show_title=\"1\" data-to_legacy_id=\"118146\" data-to_url=\"/api/aucegypt/catalog/32/course/61555/\">FILM 2120</a>.</li>\r\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">A minimum grade of B in either <a href=\"#\" class=\"permalink\" data-permalink_id=\"59744\" data-legacy_id=\"1502\" data-signature=\"e55f8fd86cfcc717f61ebb3c8812f327\" data-display_type=\"tooltip\" data-link_text=\"%prefix% %code%\" data-anchor_text=\"\" data-from_id=\"5008\" data-from_type=\"program\" data-to_id=\"62993\" data-to_type=\"course\" data-show_title=\"1\" data-to_legacy_id=\"119477\" data-to_url=\"/api/aucegypt/catalog/32/course/62993/\">FILM 2121</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"permalink\" data-permalink_id=\"59745\" data-legacy_id=\"1528\" data-signature=\"33fceef4438012fb32b0618feeb0b02e\" data-display_type=\"tooltip\" data-link_text=\"%prefix% %code%\" data-anchor_text=\"\" data-from_id=\"5008\" data-from_type=\"program\" data-to_id=\"62992\" data-to_type=\"course\" data-show_title=\"1\" data-to_legacy_id=\"119476\" data-to_url=\"/api/aucegypt/catalog/32/course/62992/\">FILM 2123</a>.</li>\r\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">A decision regarding the declaration is made following a portfolio-based interview with the applicant.</li>\r\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Students who do not pass the first interview can sit for another interview after they complete a third Introductory Required Course from either <a href=\"#\" class=\"permalink\" data-permalink_id=\"59744\" data-legacy_id=\"1502\" data-signature=\"e55f8fd86cfcc717f61ebb3c8812f327\" data-display_type=\"tooltip\" data-link_text=\"%prefix% %code%\" data-anchor_text=\"\" data-from_id=\"5008\" data-from_type=\"program\" data-to_id=\"62993\" data-to_type=\"course\" data-show_title=\"1\" data-to_legacy_id=\"119477\" data-to_url=\"/api/aucegypt/catalog/32/course/62993/\">FILM 2121</a> or <a href=\"#\" class=\"permalink\" data-permalink_id=\"59745\" data-legacy_id=\"1528\" data-signature=\"33fceef4438012fb32b0618feeb0b02e\" data-display_type=\"tooltip\" data-link_text=\"%prefix% %code%\" data-anchor_text=\"\" data-from_id=\"5008\" data-from_type=\"program\" data-to_id=\"62992\" data-to_type=\"course\" data-show_title=\"1\" data-to_legacy_id=\"119476\" data-to_url=\"/api/aucegypt/catalog/32/course/62992/\">FILM 2123</a> with a minimum grade of 'B'.</li>\r\n\t<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">The decision that follows the second interview is final.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h4 style=\"text-align: justify;\">Degree Requirements</h4>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A total of 120 credits is required for the bachelor's degree in Film in the following areas: I. Core Curriculum (37 credits), II. Film Concentration Requirements (48 - 51 credits), III. Collateral Requirements (9 credits), IV. General Electives (23-26 credits).</p>\r\n",
